  "content": {
    "text": "Micron (MU) stock hit a new all-time high on Monday after the company's deal with Anthropic (ANTH.PVT) was announced. Yahoo Finance Senior Business Reporter Ines Ferré takes a closer look in the video above.\nMicron at new all-time highs, the stock up about 5% today. Up at session highs after the company announced a deal with Anthropic where Anthropic is securing multi-year supply. Also, the goal is for these two companies to work together to co-design high bandwidth memory, and also Micron is investing in Anthropic as well. So that could be very bullish for Micron investors if Anthropic goes public and the valuation there.\nIf you take a look at the stock year to date, it's up more than uh 300% uh year to date. So it's been quite a run-up for this stock. The big earnings test though will be this Wednesday when Micron announces its quarterly results. This has become an infrastructure play that is an indispensable sort of infrastructure play when you talk about the AI trade.\nAll eyes are going to be on their supply guidance, on pricing trends, on their gross margins. And I would venture to say that if we've seen Nvidia as the big player, this is really rivaling this uh Nvidia as well, just because of the a sheer immensity of this company, its trillion dollar valuation, the the big runup that we've seen with this stock over the last uh couple of years.\nYou've got now UBS that's putting a $1,500 price target on this stock. Wall Street overwhelmingly bullish. But I will say also that you have traders that have been in the options market that have been betting that there could be a pullback. So even if they do beat, historically, Micron is one of these stocks where they beat, but it sometimes gets the sell the news kind of pressure on the stock.\nSo you have traders that are positioned as well for that. But certainly this has been a leader of the S&P 500 this year that has been really guiding the S&P 500 higher and also has been a leader among the chip space. You've got Sandisk also that is at all-time high, you've got SK Hynix, a Samsung, also these companies, it's peers. So a lot of it will be riding on the earnings report this Wednesday, Josh.",
    "text_blocks": [
      "Micron (MU) stock hit a new all-time high on Monday after the company's deal with Anthropic (ANTH.PVT) was announced. Yahoo Finance Senior Business Reporter Ines Ferré takes a closer look in the video above.",
      "Micron at new all-time highs, the stock up about 5% today. Up at session highs after the company announced a deal with Anthropic where Anthropic is securing multi-year supply. Also, the goal is for these two companies to work together to co-design high bandwidth memory, and also Micron is investing in Anthropic as well. So that could be very bullish for Micron investors if Anthropic goes public and the valuation there.",
      "If you take a look at the stock year to date, it's up more than uh 300% uh year to date. So it's been quite a run-up for this stock. The big earnings test though will be this Wednesday when Micron announces its quarterly results. This has become an infrastructure play that is an indispensable sort of infrastructure play when you talk about the AI trade.",
      "All eyes are going to be on their supply guidance, on pricing trends, on their gross margins. And I would venture to say that if we've seen Nvidia as the big player, this is really rivaling this uh Nvidia as well, just because of the a sheer immensity of this company, its trillion dollar valuation, the the big runup that we've seen with this stock over the last uh couple of years.",
      "You've got now UBS that's putting a $1,500 price target on this stock. Wall Street overwhelmingly bullish. But I will say also that you have traders that have been in the options market that have been betting that there could be a pullback. So even if they do beat, historically, Micron is one of these stocks where they beat, but it sometimes gets the sell the news kind of pressure on the stock.",
      "So you have traders that are positioned as well for that. But certainly this has been a leader of the S&P 500 this year that has been really guiding the S&P 500 higher and also has been a leader among the chip space. You've got Sandisk also that is at all-time high, you've got SK Hynix, a Samsung, also these companies, it's peers. So a lot of it will be riding on the earnings report this Wednesday, Josh."
    ],
